    "decision": "The complete original autocomplete patch adds one real timer turn and render pass to the modern async flushPosition helper used by the reposition-on-options-change regression. All183 case names and444 assertion statements are preserved in that upstream file, but scheduling changes; this is not type-only. The complete retained legacy spec has the corresponding below/above positioning assertions in a fakeAsync test using tick, simulateZoneExit and the original legacy form-field/panel selectors. It has no async flushPosition helper. Keep that historical test and all assertions. Do not copy a modern Safari retry into a different scheduler without an observed failure. Actual Safari and artifact execution of the retained regression remain required; no cross-browser or inherited-fix claim follows from this source decision.",
